# 2. Primary architecture requirement

The final attendance pipeline must follow this hierarchy:

```text
Camera frames
     |
     v
Frame sampling
     |
     v
Face observations
     |
     +---- quality
     +---- PAD
     +---- recognition evidence
     |
     v
Temporary face tracks
     |
     v
Track-level aggregation
     |
     v
One result per student per window
     |
     v
Window A / Window B / Window C
     |
     v
2-out-of-3 voting
     |
     v
Final attendance state
```

The system must NOT do:

```text
single frame
   -> recognized
   -> attendance immediately
```

Attendance must only be committed after the required temporal/window-level decision.

---

# 3. Triple-window requirement

The intended architecture is:

```text
Window A = first 5 minutes
Window B = middle 5 minutes
Window C = final 5 minutes
```

For a one-hour lecture:

```text
09:00 - 09:05  -> Window A
09:27 - 09:32  -> Window B
09:55 - 10:00  -> Window C
```

Verify the actual scheduler.

If the live implementation still only has Window A and Window B, implement Window C consistently rather than merely changing documentation.

Each window must produce one student-level result.

The voting unit is the completed window, not an individual frame.

Example:

```text
Student 17

A -> PRESENT
B -> UNRESOLVED
C -> PRESENT

Final -> PRESENT
```

Do not allow one frame from Window A to override the complete results of B and C.

---

# 4. No single-frame attendance

Inspect the exact attendance commit path.

The desired flow is:

```text
sample observations
     |
     v
collect evidence
     |
     v
aggregate identity
     |
     v
aggregate PAD/liveness
     |
     v
apply security gates
     |
     v
produce one window result
     |
     v
record attendance once
```

If `record_window_attendance()` or an equivalent function is called inside the per-frame loop, fix it.

Attendance persistence must be idempotent for:

```text
student + slot + window
```

Repeated observations of the same student must not create repeated attendance records.

