# 5. Classroom face tracking

The camera will be mounted at the front of the classroom.

Students in the back rows can occupy fewer pixels than students in the front.

Do not treat:

```text
small face in one frame
```

as:

```text
absent
```

Use three conceptual quality levels:

```text
RECOGNITION_SAFE
TRACKABLE_BUT_SMALL
UNUSABLE
```

## RECOGNITION_SAFE

The face has enough usable detail for normal recognition/PAD processing.

## TRACKABLE_BUT_SMALL

The face can be detected and tracked, but recognition from that observation is not reliable enough.

Keep the track.

Store bounded evidence.

Wait for later observations.

Example:

```text
Frame 1 -> small
Frame 2 -> small
Frame 3 -> recognition-safe
Frame 4 -> blurry
Frame 5 -> recognition-safe
```

Recognition should use Frames 3 and 5.

## UNUSABLE

The observation is not reliable enough for tracking or biometric processing.

Do not force an identity.

Do not mark the person absent merely because of this frame.

