# 11. Camera pipeline and lag

The camera preview must remain responsive.

Preferred architecture:

```text
Camera acquisition
       |
       +-----------------> preview
       |
       v
latest-frame buffer
       |
       v
controlled inference sampling
       |
       +----> detection
       +----> PAD
       +----> recognition
       +----> tracking
```

Avoid unbounded queues.

Prefer the newest useful frame.

Do not initialize InsightFace/PAD models inside the frame loop.

Do not run database writes on every frame.

Do not introduce excessive threading if the existing architecture can solve the issue with a simple latest-frame design.

Measure performance if practical.

---

# 12. Camera resolution must remain configurable

The current configuration may use 640x480.

Do not assume this is the final deployment resolution.

The final hardware is expected to use a high-quality USB-UVC camera module, potentially 4K.

Do not simply feed every 4K frame into every model.

Prefer:

```text
high-resolution camera
      |
      v
capture / preview
      |
      v
efficient detection resolution
      |
      v
high-quality face crop
      |
      +---- recognition
      +---- PAD
```

Preserve source detail where it matters.

Keep camera resolution configurable.

